  <data name="TPM_WhatIsTPMDescription" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A Trusted Platform Module (TPM) is a microchip designed to provide basic security-related functions, primarily involving encryption keys. TPMs are usually installed on the computer's motherboard and communicate with the rest of the system using a hardware bus. Computers integrated with TPM can create cryptographic keys and encrypt them so that they can only be decrypted by the TPM. This process is called wrapping or binding the keys.</value>
